# WhatsApp approval — setup guide (Phase 2)

**Kyun WhatsApp:** Telegram Pakistan me blocked hai, is liye approval channel **WhatsApp Cloud API**
(Meta ki official API) par shift ho raha hai. Koi unofficial bridge / browser automation / scraped session
nahi — sirf Meta ka official Cloud API.

> Status: **setup guide ab**, implementation **phase2.mjs** me (agla phase).
> Jo kaam Meta ki taraf se pending hai (business verification, number verification) wo din le sakta hai,
> is liye yeh document pehle de raha hoon taake aap parallel me setup shuru kar sakein.

---

## 1. Free kaise rahega (2026 ki asli pricing)

| Cheez | Cost |
| --- | --- |
| Cloud API access, WABA, webhook | **Free** |
| Service messages (non-template replies inside a 24-hour customer window) | **1 000 free per business number per month**, uske baad billed |
| Template messages (marketing / utility / authentication) | **Billed from the first message** |
| Messages jo customer (aap) bhejte hain | **Free** |
| Reactions | Free, 1 000 ke count me nahi |

**Isliye design yeh hai (100% free path):**

1. Post ready hone par **email** jata hai (Resend — already free, 100/day) jisme ek
   **“Approve on WhatsApp”** button hota hai: `https://wa.me/<business-number>?text=APR-<code>`.
2. Aap us button ko dabate hain → WhatsApp khulta hai, message pehle se likha hota hai → **Send**.
   Aapka inbound message 24-ghante ka **customer service window** khol deta hai (inbound always free).
3. Usi window me bot **free-form reply** karta hai: post ka text + `✅ Approve` / `❌ Reject` buttons.
   Yeh service message hai → free tier ke andar (din me 1–2 message, mahine me ~60).
4. Button tap → webhook → same approval token system (single-use, expiry, audit log) → publish.

Optional (agar aap chahein): **utility template** se bot khud pehle message bhej de — lekin wo per-message
billed hai (Pakistan ke liye cents me). Default OFF rahega, settings me “WhatsApp: paid template mode”.

---

## 2. Meta side setup (ek baar)

### 2.1 Accounts

1. <https://business.facebook.com> par **Meta Business portfolio** banayein (free).
2. <https://developers.facebook.com> → **Create app** → type **Business** → apna portfolio select karein.
3. App dashboard → **Add product → WhatsApp → Set up**.

### 2.2 Number

- Ek phone number chahiye jo **currently WhatsApp par registered na ho** (spare SIM best hai — dobara
  WhatsApp app me login karna ho to Cloud API se delete karna padega).
- Pakistan ke numbers supported hain. Verification SMS/call se hoti hai.
- Test ke liye Meta ek free **test number** bhi deta hai (sirf 5 verified recipients tak) — shuruat isse
  kar sakte hain, baad me apna number add kar lein.

### 2.3 IDs aur token

WhatsApp → **API Setup** se yeh 3 cheezein note karein:

| Value | Kahaan milegi | Env var |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Phone number ID | API Setup → “Phone number ID” | `WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID` |
| WABA ID | API Setup | (sirf reference) |
| Temporary token (24h) | API Setup | testing ke liye |

**Permanent token (production ke liye zaroori):** Business settings → **System users** → Add → role *Admin*
→ *Generate new token* → app select karein → permissions: `whatsapp_business_messaging`,
`whatsapp_business_management` → token copy karein → `WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN`.

### 2.4 Webhook

App → WhatsApp → **Configuration → Webhook**:

- **Callback URL:** `https://<APP_BASE_URL host>/api/v1/integrations/whatsapp/webhook`
- **Verify token:** koi bhi random string (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 16`) → same value
  `WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN` me daalein
- **Webhook fields:** `messages` subscribe karein
- App → Settings → Basic → **App secret** → `WHATSAPP_APP_SECRET`
  (webhook signature `X-Hub-Signature-256` verify karne ke liye — bina iske koi bhi fake request bhej sakta hai)

### 2.5 Owner number

`WHATSAPP_OWNER_NUMBER` = aapka personal WhatsApp number, country code ke sath, sirf digits
(e.g. `923001234567`). Sirf isi number se aane wale messages accept honge.

---

## 3. Env vars (phase2 ke baad)

```bash
WHATSAPP_PHONE_NUMBER_ID=
WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN=
WHATSAPP_VERIFY_TOKEN=
WHATSAPP_APP_SECRET=
WHATSAPP_OWNER_NUMBER=
WHATSAPP_API_VERSION=v21.0
WHATSAPP_TEMPLATE_MODE=off        # off = sirf free 24h window (default)
```

Yeh Worker secrets honge: `npx wrangler secret put WHATSAPP_ACCESS_TOKEN` (waise hi baaki).

---

## 4. Security model (phase2 me implement hoga)

- Webhook par **`X-Hub-Signature-256` HMAC verify** (app secret) — warna reject.
- Sirf `WHATSAPP_OWNER_NUMBER` se aane wale messages process honge.
- Buttons me **raw approval token nahi** jayega — ek short-lived **approval code** (10 min, single use,
  DB me hashed) jo server par token se map hota hai.
- Approval phir bhi wahi purana system: single-use, expiry-checked, POST-only, audit-logged.
- Koi bhi text message (jaise “approve”) sirf tab kaam karega jab wo owner ke number se ho aur code match kare.
- Replay protection: har inbound `message.id` DB me record hota hai; duplicate webhook retries ignore.

---

## 5. Free-tier limits (honest)

| Limit | Value | Hamara use |
| --- | --- | --- |
| Service messages | 1 000 / number / month free | ~60–90 / month |
| 24-hour window | Aapke message ke baad hi khulta hai | Email link se message bhejte hain |
| Templates | Billed per message | Default off |
| Number | 1 business number enough | 1 |
| Verification | SMS/call, business verification may be requested for higher limits | chhote use ke liye usually nahi |

Agar aap chahein ke bot **bina aapke message** ke khud message bheje, to utility template + payment method
chahiye hoga (billed, cents/month). Yeh optional hoga, default nahi.

---

## 6. Jab phase2 aayega

`phase2.mjs` yeh karega:

1. `WhatsAppGateway` adapter (Cloud API: send text, interactive buttons, mark read) + local stub
2. Webhook route: GET verify (hub.challenge) + POST with signature check
3. Approval email me “Approve on WhatsApp” link (existing token → short code)
4. Dashboard → Settings → Integrations me WhatsApp card (Connect = credentials check, Test = message aapke number par)
5. Wahi audit trail: `whatsapp.inbound`, `whatsapp.reply_sent`, `approval.approved` (channel: whatsapp)
6. Tests: signature reject, wrong number reject, expired code, replay, approve/reject happy path

Jab tak phase2 nahi aata, email approval poora kaam karta hai — kuch bhi block nahi hai.
